# 6. REMOVE RESOLUTION CASE WORKFLOW

The customer explicitly rejected unnecessary ambiguous-case handling.

Retire the active review dependency on:

- Resolution Hub.
- ResolutionCase creation.
- Escalate to Resolution.
- Ambiguous-case queue.
- ResolutionCase classification.
- Separate Committee resolution decision.
- Special resolution status requirements for normal review completion.
- AI automatic escalation suggestions that create a case.

## Important distinction

Removing ResolutionCase does NOT mean that all evidence must be clearly valid or invalid.

A reviewer may still encounter:

- Insufficient evidence.
- Missing information.
- Conflicting dates.
- Incomplete academic records.
- Inconsistent volunteer participation.
- Unclear declaration details.

These conditions remain valid review observations.

They must be handled using the existing normal workflow:

- Record reviewer observations.
- Request scoped supplementation when appropriate.
- Keep the review pending when there is not enough information to complete it.
- Record an authorized negative assessment when supported by actual verified facts and applicable rules.

Do not automatically reject an application merely because an old ResolutionCase is no longer available.

Do not automatically mark unresolved evidence as accepted.

Do not create a replacement "special case" subsystem under a different name.

